/**
 * Config.gs — Golden Griffins Inventory
 * ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
 * App constants, the database schema, and the default (seed) values.
 *
 * How the schema works:
 *   - Each entry in TABLES is one sheet (tab) in the spreadsheet.
 *   - Columns are always found by their HEADER NAME, never by position, so you
 *     can reorder columns in the sheet without breaking anything.
 *   - Adding a column here and re-running setupDatabase() adds it to the sheet.
 *   - Never rename an existing column name here without renaming the header
 *     in the sheet too (the data would appear to vanish).
 *
 * Column types:
 *   id        unique record ID (generated by the server)
 *   string    one line of text            text      multi-line text
 *   int       whole number                number    decimal number
 *   bool      TRUE / FALSE                date      ISO timestamp text
 *   enum      one of a fixed list         json      structured data
 *   ref       ID of a row in another table
 *   refList   several IDs, stored as "ID1|ID2|ID3"
 *   measure   a size typed by people, e.g. 1/8 or 1 1/2 (a numeric copy is
 *             kept in the companion "...Value" column for sorting/filtering)
 *
 * system: true  → only the server sets this value; anything sent by the
 *                 browser for that field is ignored.
 */

